(text "RASPBERRY PI 5 DOMAIN  (relays, presence sensors, RTC)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 16.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "23109987-f04c-44df-8f7a-c69491e654e9"))
(text "ESP32 DOMAIN  (11x PZEM-004T via 2x CD74HC4067, 2x aircon IR, 3.3V logic)" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 15.24 149.86 0) (effects (font (size 1.8 1.8) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4676b9d7-7371-42f9-be34-5755fc6170a6"))
(text "WIRING NOTES\n1. Same label name = same wire. Connect every pin that shares a label.\n   Full pin-to-pin list: NETLIST.md\n2. J1 pin numbers are PHYSICAL header pins (not BCM).\n3. K1 relay board: REMOVE the VCC/JD-VCC jumper.\n   VCC = Pi 3V3 (opto LEDs); JD-VCC + GND = PS1 (5V >=2A).\n   Do NOT tie Pi GND to K1 GND (keeps opto isolation).\n4. Relays are active-LOW: GPIO LOW = relay ON.\n   RLY01-03 drive the PFC capacitor-bank contactors.\n5. GPIO14/15 (HLK zones 1-2) are UART pins:\n   disable serial console + serial hardware.\n6. Keep SPI (GPIO7-11) and audio/PWM overlays\n   (GPIO12/13/18/19) disabled.\n7. Boot check: GPIO9-27 pull down at power-up, so relays\n   may click ON until app.py starts. Fix if needed:\n   config.txt: gpio=9-13,16-24,27=op,dh\n8. ESP32 side is all 3.3V: PZEM TTL '5V' pins and mux\n   VCC come from ESP32 3V3 (ESP_3V3). No level shifter.\n9. Two muxes, same S0-S3 wires: Mux A sends the selected\n   PZEM TX to ESP32 RX1, Mux B sends ESP32 TX1 to that\n   PZEM RX only. Channel Cn = PZEM #n on BOTH muxes.\n10. Both mux EN = GND (always on). C11-C15 unused.\n    IR modules: VCC = ESP32 5V/VIN (USB_VBUS).\n11. Control wiring only: mains side not shown." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 299.72 16.51 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "4d895aeb-124b-42df-87d9-8d4f583dfc0d"))
